b69c-95d4cfd71254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351533 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=1,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351803 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351803 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351803 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a5e97c5-f73a-5dc7-aca2-86493283b121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351913 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351913 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351913 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "259df9a5-e148-52b1-8c76-e5f3797156f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352507 #edb/ref 1080 "$A$ is not diagonalizable" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352507 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352507 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6a0b1af0-e162-51c8-a699-561daf399c7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352816 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{a